Z||000002||Red2m4||12-02-2000||05:45 PM||||I HAD a palmI, the original, paid $50 for it from my old boss.  I liked it for storing phone numbers, addresses and such.  Was also good for a notepad.  The script that you use to enter info is kind of a pain, but not too hard to learn.  If you get one, i would recomend the newer ones as they have many more features. There is also a fair amount of software on the net you can download.  There was also a keyboard attachment that I've seen used and that would be extremely useful if you plan on doing  serious note-taking or writing.<P>   Alas, I no longer have it, it broke, probably becuase I stored it in the console (armrest) Compartment of my fiero over the summer and it melted the guts, I think.<P>   I would buy another though.<BR>||||reg||1
